ct only when the comparison is true.\\n5. EXTRACTION (architect 2.3): Write to `references/{slug}.md` under the target file's own directory, `{slug}` kebab-case from the procedure name; Edit the target to replace the diagram block with the context-pointer sentence; re-run the token check once to confirm the count dropped, and report a residual over-threshold count as a fact without looping or extracting unrelated content.\\n\\nEncode this as a Mermaid flowchart in the agent file. The architect spec's own flowchart in Section 2 is the reference shape \\u2014 every branch and terminal state in it must appear. House-style rewording is allowed; dropping a branch is not.\",\"objective\":\"Turn Step 6 of `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` from today's unconditional binary (edit inline, or return a fenced block) into the ordered decision procedure specified in architecture spec Sections 1, 2, 2.1, 2.2, and 2.3 \\u2014 including the Mermaid flowchart that encodes it.\",\"constraints\":\"- Target agent identifier is `process-siren:process-siren`. NEVER write `plugin-creator:process-siren` anywhere.\\n- Never hardcode 4400. The threshold is read at decision time via `uvx --from skilllint python -c \\\"from skilllint.limits import BODY_TOKEN_WARNING; print(BODY_TOKEN_WARNING)\\\"`. Use BODY_TOKEN_WARNING, not BODY_TOKEN_ERROR (R5).\\n- The token count command is `uvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only {target-file}`. Do not parse full `skilllint check` output or match on SK006/AS005 finding text \\u2014 that is brittle against wording changes across versions.\\n- Tier classification is evaluated BEFORE the token count is known. Preserve that ordering explicitly in the flowchart; it is what removes the agent's incentive to outcome-shop a tier (R2).\\n- Tooling fail-safe (R3): if either command exits non-zero or stdout is not a bare integer, do not retry and do not extract \\u2014 leave the diagram inline (today's exact behavior) and record the failure and reason 