with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-27T06:03:00.239349+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Read architect spec Sections 3 and 4, then read the current `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` including T1's new Step 6. Add:\\n\\n1. EXTRACTED FILE SHAPE (architect Section 3): the `references/{slug}.md` layout \\u2014 `# {Procedure Title} \\u2014 {Owning Document Name}` heading, the standard `> [!IMPORTANT]` admonition block, the procedure-label sentence, then the fenced Mermaid diagram. State outright that this is a `.md` file and never a bare `.mmd`/`.mermaid` file.\\n2. ADMONITION DEDUP: existing Step 7 (~line 226) already branches on \\\"if this is a `references/*.md` file\\\". Confirm and state that an extracted file inherits that check against its OWNING SKILL.md, not only against itself, so the admonition is not duplicated across the pair. This is a confirmation of existing logic, not new logic \\u2014 do not rewrite Step 7's dedup rule.\\n3. CONTEXT-POINTER TEMPLATE (architect Section 4): `{Opening words stating the branch/condition that reaches it}, consult [{Procedure Title}](./references/{slug}.md) \\u2014 {one-line description of what the extracted diagram covers}.` State that the opening-words clause is mandatory, not decoration: a reader must be able to tell from the sentence alone whether their current situation is the one that needs the pointer, without following it speculatively. Instruct that the opening words are derived from the same tier-3 lead-in language that classified the diagram in Step 6 \\u2014 the condition that made it tier 3 is the condition that belongs in the pointer.\\n4. CONTRADICTION RESOLUTION (item #3244 \\\"Correction\\\", second paragraph): the agent file today says both \\\"replace the original content with the diagram\\\" and \\\"surgical replacement of the original section with the diagram, preserving surrounding content.\\\" Neither sentence resolves the case where a diagram is ADDED as a new section alongside step prose that stays in place \\u2014 and that unhandled case is exactly what accrues duplication. State the resolution explicitly in the file: which content is replaced, which is preserved, and that content added alongside surviving prose hands off to the duplication check. Do not leave the resolution implicit.\",\"objective\":\"Give the extraction branch a concrete output shape: the required `references/*.md` file layout (architect Section 3), the context-pointer sentence template (architect Section 4), the Step 7 admonition-dedup confirmation, and an explicit resolution of the file's own internal contradiction between \\\"replace the original content with the diagram\\\" (~line 219) and \\\"preserving surrounding content\\\" (~line 313).\",\"constraints\":\"- Target agent identifier is `process-siren:process-siren`; never `plugin-creator:process-siren`.\\n- The admonition block text is fixed \\u2014 reproduce it exactly as it already appears in the agent file / architect Section 3. Do not reword it.\\n- Do not re-open Step 6's decision logic (T1's scope) or write the duplication-check procedure itself (T3's scope). This task states only that the added-alongside case routes to the duplication check.\\n- The extracted file must never be a bare `.mmd`/`.mermaid` file \\u2014 say so in words the AC4 check can match.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"An edited `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` carrying the extracted-file shape, the context-pointer template, the confirmed admonition-dedup scope, and the explicit replace-vs-preserve resolution.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. The `references/{slug}.md` file shape is fully specified \\u2014 heading, admonition block, procedure-label sentence, fenced diagram \\u2014 and matches architect Section 3.\\n2. The agent file states in words that an extracted diagram is a 