e the added-alongside case, or does it restate both sentences and leave it open? (Required: it decides.)\\n- Q4: Did I invent any new admonition-dedup logic instead of confirming what Step 7 already does? (Required answer: no.)\",\"handoff\":\"Report the section headings added and where the added-alongside case hands off, so T3 can attach the duplication check at that exact point.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"},{\"id\":\"T3\",\"title\":\"Add the duplication check and the per-diagram disposition report contract to process-siren.md\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"plugin-creator:ai-doc-optimizer\",\"dependencies\":[\"T2\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-27T06:03:00.239368+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Read architect spec Sections 2.4 and 5 and item #3244's Design Note section 19.1 (the sharper correction), then read the current agent file including T1's and T2's edits.\\n\\nDUPLICATION CHECK (Step 6.4) \\u2014 runs after placement for EVERY diagram this invocation authored, tier 1 or 3, inline or extracted. Not tier-3-only.\\n\\nDecision test: does the target document, at a location this invocation did NOT edit, contain prose (numbered steps, a bulleted sequence, or an earlier diagram) stating the same branching/sequencing the just-authored diagram now encodes?\\n- No overlap \\u2192 nothing to do. This is the common case; say so, so the agent does not manufacture findings.\\n- Overlap that THIS invocation introduced (the diagram is new content added alongside pre-existing prose this invocation read but did not replace or edit) \\u2192 RESOLVE it: edit the overlapping prose down to only the detail the notation cannot carry \\u2014 exact call signatures, payload shapes, schema/field pointers \\u2014 removing the restated branching/sequencing. This is authorized deletion because the agent created the duplicate and owns cleanup of its own output.\\n- Overlap that PREDATES this invocation \\u2192 REPORT ONLY, never delete (R4, Anti-Goal 1). Name the file, section, and overlapping content in the disposition report for the caller to resolve.\\n\\nState why the distinguishing fact is observable rather than a judgment call: \\\"did my own Step 6 edit in this same invocation create this overlap\\\" is directly readable from the agent's own action log within the current run, and needs no new tooling.\\n\\nGround the rule in the design principle (item Design Note 19.1): agents parse Mermaid as notation and never see a rendered picture, so the diagram is the sole authoritative representation of sequencing and branching, and prose restating the same branches is waste plus a second source of truth that can disagree.\\n\\nDISPOSITION REPORT (architect Section 5) \\u2014 every invocation reaching Step 6 emits one fixed-shape line per diagram placed, in its existing report (standalone mode) or its Step 6/7 completion note (file mode):\\n\\n`Diagram: {procedure name} | Tier: {1|3|n/a-file-creation} | Placement: {inline|extracted to references/{slug}.md} | Reason: {threshold comparison TOKENS/THRESHOLD, or file-creation-mode, or tooling-failure-fail-safe} | Duplication: {none | resolved (edited {location}) | reported (pre-existing, see {location})}`\\n\\nState that this is a fixed-shape line, not a narrative summary, so a caller \\u2014 human or `process-siren:woo-sailor` \\u2014 can scan many dispositions without re-deriving them.\",\"objective\":\"Implement architect Sections 2.4 and 5: the prose-vs-diagram duplication check with its introduced-vs-pre-existing split, and the fixed-shape disposition line that makes every placement and de-duplication decision observable.\",\"constraints\":\"- Never delete or edit prose whose duplication predates this invocation. R4 exists because a wrong r